// Hand-authored (2026-07-25): EXCIMER LASER beam tile, 96x3 RGBA.
// Generated, not painted — the recipe is in the commit message. Rows are the
// beam's cross-section (fringe / hot core / fringe) mapped across
// `presentation.line.width`; the 96 columns tile every 96 world px
// (`length: 96`, i.e. one texel per world pixel, so the crackle is genuinely
// per-pixel). Colors come from what it replaces: smoke_puff's s76_2 dots
// (#f0f0b4 / #f4f470) over laser_pulse's splinter colour 75 (#ecb400), with
// white-hot sparks. Alpha carries the intensity profile — the beam draws
// additively (SRC_ALPHA, ONE) when the lit look is on, plain alpha otherwise.
{
  "frames": 1,
  "origin": [
    0,
    0
  ]
}
